==Battleground==
*1 [[Puffsley's Comet]] spawns as the boss after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*3 [[Corporal Weyland]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 40~50 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,500f</sup>.
*1 [[Project A]] spawns after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*4 [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*4 [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*4 [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 160 seconds<sup>4,800f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*4 [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 206.67 seconds<sup>6,200f</sup>, delay 40~50 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
You don't have the luxury of having Rich Cat avaliable for Puffsley, so manage your money carefully. [[Can Can Cat]] is very strong here, being able to deal heavy damage against the Star Peng horde and even apply Slow to Puffsley if you got Can Can's Target Alien talent. [[Seafarer Cat]] is, as per usual, strong here, acting as both a strong CC unit and an Area Attacker. Add [[Catellite]] as your main defence option, and any Ubers you might've added for anti-Alien damage, and this stage should be easily done.

==Trivia==
*Puffer Planet's Japanese name, River Pig Planet (リバーピッグプラネット), refers to how the Japanese word for pufferfish, 河豚 ''fugu'', literally translates to "river pig".
**It may also be a reference to the video game series [[wikipedia:LittleBigPlanet|''LittleBigPlanet'']] (リトルビッグプラネット), whose name is quite similar in Japanese.

